    "title": "De-risking Monolith Modernization with the Strangler Fig Pattern and Apigee",
    "scenario": "An enterprise operates a massive monolithic on-premises banking application. The architecture leadership mandates migrating to cloud-native microservices on Google Cloud. A 'big bang' complete rewrite is deemed too high-risk by the executive board. What incremental modernization pattern and Google Cloud component should be deployed?",
    "keywords": [
      "Strangler Fig Pattern",
      "Apigee X",
      "Monolith Modernization",
      "Incremental Migration",
      "API Facade"
    ],
    "isMultiSelect": false,
    "expectedSelectCount": 1,
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "Convert the monolith into an Excel spreadsheet.",
        "isTrap": true,
        "trapType": "manual_scripting_overhead"
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "Shut down the on-premises datacenter on Friday and deploy all new code simultaneously.",
        "isTrap": true,
        "trapType": "single_point_of_failure"
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "Implement the Strangler Fig pattern: Deploy Apigee X as an API Facade in front of the on-premises monolith, route existing API traffic through Apigee, and gradually migrate individual domain capabilities (e.g. Accounts, Payments) into Google Cloud microservices, redirecting API proxy routes incrementally until the legacy monolith is decommissioned.",
        "isTrap": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "Maintain both systems completely independent with zero synchronization for 10 years.",
        "isTrap": true,
        "trapType": "manual_scripting_overhead"
      }
    ],
    "correct": "C",
    "explanation": "The Strangler Fig pattern places an API gateway (Apigee X) in front of legacy systems. Individual functionalities are gradually carved out into cloud microservices. The API gateway updates its routes incrementally, de-risking the migration and ensuring zero downtime for consumers.",
    "distractors": {
      "A": "Spreadsheets cannot support enterprise banking transactions.",
      "B": "Big-bang migrations have catastrophic failure rates and high business risk.",
      "C": "Correct. The Strangler Fig pattern with Apigee X API facade enables safe, zero-downtime incremental modernization.",
      "D": "Independent non-synchronized systems create massive data corruption and operational confusion."
    },
    "architectureComponents": [
      "Apigee X",
      "Strangler Fig Pattern",
      "Google Kubernetes Engine",
      "Cloud Run",
      "Hybrid Interconnect"
    ],
    "terraformSnippet": "resource \"google_apigee_envgroup\" \"modernization_apis\" {\n  name      = \"banking-apis-envgroup\"\n  org_id    = google_apigee_organization.apigee_org.id\n  hostnames = [\"api.bank.com\"]\n}",
