    "title": "Optimizing Multi-Region Spanner Write Latency with Leader Region Placement",
    "scenario": "An enterprise has an active-active multi-region Spanner database deployed across North America and Europe. 80% of write transactions originate from corporate headquarters in New York (us-east4), while 20% originate from London (europe-west2). To minimize write transaction latency, where should the Spanner Default Leader Region be placed?",
    "keywords": [
      "Cloud Spanner",
      "Default Leader Region",
      "Write Latency",
      "Paxos Consensus",
      "us-east4"
    ],
    "isMultiSelect": false,
    "expectedSelectCount": 1,
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "Disable the Paxos leader completely.",
        "isTrap": true,
        "trapType": "single_point_of_failure"
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "Rotate the leader region every 10 milliseconds.",
        "isTrap": true,
        "trapType": "premature_optimization"
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "Set default leader region to Tokyo (asia-northeast1).",
        "isTrap": true,
        "trapType": "premature_optimization"
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "Set the Spanner Default Leader Region to 'us-east4', ensuring that Paxos leader replicas reside physically closest to the 80% majority write traffic source, eliminating trans-Atlantic round-trips for the majority of transaction commits.",
        "isTrap": false
      }
    ],
    "correct": "D",
    "explanation": "In multi-region Cloud Spanner, write transactions must coordinate through the Paxos leader. Placing the Default Leader Region in the geographic region where the majority of write traffic originates (us-east4) minimizes network transit latency for 80% of commits.",
    "distractors": {
      "A": "Paxos distributed consensus mathematically requires a coordinator leader.",
      "B": "Rapid leader rotation causes continuous consensus disruption.",
      "C": "Placing the leader in Tokyo forces all US and European writes to make multi-continent round-trips to Asia.",
      "D": "Correct. Placing the leader in us-east4 minimizes network round-trips for the majority of write transactions."
    },
    "architectureComponents": [
      "Cloud Spanner",
      "Default Leader Region",
      "Paxos Consensus",
      "Multi-Region Topology"
    ],
    "terraformSnippet": "resource \"google_spanner_database\" \"global_leader_db\" {\n  instance = google_spanner_instance.multi_region_instance.name\n  name     = \"global_orders\"\n  ddl = [\n    \"ALTER DATABASE `global_orders` SET OPTIONS (default_leader = 'us-east4')\"\n  ]\n}",
    "officialDocUrl": "https://cloud.google.com/spanner/docs/multi-region-overview#default-leader-region",
