    "scenario": "An enterprise operates legacy worker VMs on Compute Engine. Occasionally, an internal queue processing daemon freezes without crashing the VM. The operations team wants an automated self-healing remediation pipeline: When a Cloud Monitoring alert detects zero queue message processing for 10 minutes, the alert must automatically trigger an automated workflow to safely restart the systemd service on the affected VM without human intervention. How should this be built?",
    "keywords": [
      "Cloud Monitoring Alert",
      "Webhook Notification Channel",
      "Cloud Run / Cloud Functions",
      "Automated Remediation",
      "Self-Healing"
    ],
    "isMultiSelect": false,
    "expectedSelectCount": 1,
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "Disable all queue monitoring.",
        "isTrap": true,
        "trapType": "public_ip_security_risk"
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "Hire an operator to check queue metrics manually every 5 minutes.",
        "isTrap": true,
        "trapType": "manual_scripting_overhead"
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "Reboot all 500 enterprise VMs simultaneously whenever one service freezes.",
        "isTrap": true,
        "trapType": "single_point_of_failure"
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "Attach a Webhook Notification Channel to the Cloud Monitoring Alert Policy, invoking a Cloud Function / Cloud Run service authenticated via OIDC token, which uses the Compute Engine OS Config / Cloud Workflows API to execute a remote systemd restart script on the specific VM.",
        "isTrap": false
      }
    ],
    "correct": "D",
    "explanation": "Cloud Monitoring Alert Webhooks trigger automated remediation handlers (Cloud Functions/Run). The handler parses the alert JSON payload (containing the affected VM ID) and executes targeted remediation (e.g. OS Config agent execution or VM restart) automatically.",
    "distractors": {
      "A": "Disabling monitoring blinds operations to stalled queues.",
      "B": "Manual human checks are slow, error-prone, and increase Mean Time to Recovery (MTTR).",
      "C": "Rebooting all VMs causes widespread unnecessary collateral service outages.",
      "D": "Correct. Alert Policy -> Webhook -> Cloud Function -> OS Config restart implements automated closed-loop self-healing."
    },
    "architectureComponents": [
      "Cloud Monitoring Alert Policy",
      "Webhook Notification Channel",
      "Cloud Functions",
      "OS Config API"
    ],
    "terraformSnippet": "resource \"google_monitoring_notification_channel\" \"auto_remediation_webhook\" {\n  display_name = \"Auto-Remediation Webhook\"\n  type         = \"webhook_tokenauth\"\n  labels = {\n    url = \"https://remediation-handler.run.app/alert\"\n  }\n}",
