    "scenario": "A developer is configuring a pod on GKE to write diagnostic records to a private Cloud Storage bucket. The pod runs under the Kubernetes Service Account (KSA) 'log-collector' in namespace 'monitoring'. To implement Workload Identity without static service account keys, what exact IAM binding must be applied to the Google Service Account (GSA) 'gsa-storage-writer@project.iam.gserviceaccount.com'?",
    "keywords": [
      "Workload Identity",
      "GKE",
      "roles/iam.workloadIdentityUser",
      "KSA to GSA Binding"
    ],
    "isMultiSelect": false,
    "expectedSelectCount": 1,
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "Grant roles/owner to all users in the project.",
        "isTrap": true,
        "trapType": "primitive_iam_overprivileged"
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "Grant the role roles/iam.workloadIdentityUser to member 'serviceAccount:project.svc.id.goog[monitoring/log-collector]' on the Google Service Account 'gsa-storage-writer@project.iam.gserviceaccount.com', and annotate the KSA with the GSA email.",
        "isTrap": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "Download a private key JSON file and mount it via a ConfigMap.",
        "isTrap": true,
        "trapType": "public_ip_security_risk"
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "Disable IAM authentication on the Cloud Storage bucket.",
        "isTrap": true,
        "trapType": "public_ip_security_risk"
      }
    ],
    "correct": "B",
    "explanation": "GKE Workload Identity connects Kubernetes Service Accounts (KSAs) to Google Service Accounts (GSAs). The GSA must grant roles/iam.workloadIdentityUser to the principal serviceAccount:PROJECT_ID.svc.id.goog[NAMESPACE/KSA_NAME], and the KSA must be annotated with iam.gke.io/gcp-service-account.",
    "distractors": {
      "A": "Granting project Owner violates least-privilege principles and creates extreme security vulnerability.",
      "B": "Correct. Binding roles/iam.workloadIdentityUser to serviceAccount:PROJECT.svc.id.goog[NAMESPACE/KSA] enables secure keyless Workload Identity.",
      "C": "Static JSON keys in ConfigMaps leak credentials and fail modern security controls.",
      "D": "Disabling bucket IAM exposes corporate storage to public unauthorized reading and writing."
    },
    "architectureComponents": [
      "Google Kubernetes Engine",
      "Workload Identity",
      "Cloud IAM",
      "Kubernetes Service Account"
    ],
    "terraformSnippet": "resource \"google_service_account_iam_member\" \"workload_identity_binding\" {\n  service_account_id = google_service_account.gsa.name\n  role               = \"roles/iam.workloadIdentityUser\"\n  member             = \"serviceAccount:my-project.svc.id.goog[monitoring/log-collector]\"\n}",
